{"timestamp": "2026-01-12T13:23:38.987840", "level": "INFO", "event": "heuristic_reflection_completed", "data": {"experience_lessons": "The previous logic of ranking INA candidates solely by total gradient volume traversing each switch, without considering Pod-level traffic imbalance and cross-Pod congestion patterns, failed to prevent critical Core-layer bottlenecks. This caused excessive cross-Pod traffic to concentrate on a few high-traffic links (e.g., Aggr→Core), leading to 100% saturation despite INA deployment. Additionally, the worker assignment heuristic prioritized local Pod switches without enforcing load balancing across INA nodes, resulting in underutilized INA switches and idle PS nodes, which indicates that the assignment logic did not account for the physical bandwidth hierarchy and oversubscription ratio. The failure to model the 2:1 oversubscription constraint in the scoring and routing logic led to inefficient aggregation placement and routing, ultimately causing makespan degradation.", "functions_to_update": ["_select_ina_candidates", "_assign_workers_to_aggregators", "solve_with_heuristic"]}}
